---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
const research = (await getCollection('work')).filter(p=>['human-ai-collaboration','synthetic-pilot-lab','protein-language-models'].includes(p.id)).sort((a,b)=>a.data.order-b.data.order);
---
<Layout title="Research — Ashmit Mukherjee" description="Human–AI interaction, multi-agent simulation, synthetic experiment pilots, and rigorous model evaluation. Research and manuscript by Ashmit Mukherjee at NYU Abu Dhabi.">
  <div class="container research-page">
    <header class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Research</p><h1>Research</h1><p>I am a Computer Science senior at NYU Abu Dhabi, interested in human–AI interaction, multi-agent systems, and computational approaches to studying collective decisions.</p><div class="inline-links"><a class="text-link" href="/work/">All projects ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="mailto:asm8879@nyu.edu">Get in touch ↗</a></div></header>
    <section class="section research-questions" aria-labelledby="questions-heading"><div class="section-head"><h2 id="questions-heading">Research interests</h2></div><div class="question-grid"><article><span class="project-number">01</span><h3>Advice &amp; interaction</h3><p>How does AI advice affect cooperation, coordination, and individual agency when decisions involve multiple people and agents?</p></article><article><span class="project-number">02</span><h3>Simulation &amp; its limits</h3><p>When can synthetic pilots expose problems in an experimental design, and what requires evidence from human participants?</p></article><article><span class="project-number">03</span><h3>Evidence &amp; evaluation</h3><p>How can controlled comparisons, retained records, and explicit failure handling make AI-supported conclusions easier to assess?</p></article></div></section>
    <section class="section research-projects" aria-labelledby="current-heading"><div class="section-head"><h2 id="current-heading">Research projects</h2></div>{research.map((p,i)=><article class="project-row"><span class="project-number">0{i+1}</span><div><p class="eyebrow">{p.data.status}</p><h3><a href={`/work/${p.id}/`}>{p.data.title}</a></h3><p>{p.data.summary}</p><p class="research-role">{p.data.role} · {p.data.organization}</p></div><a class="row-link" href={`/work/${p.id}/`} aria-label={`Read ${p.data.title}`}>↗</a></article>)}</section>
    <section class="section split" id="manuscript"><div><p class="eyebrow">Manuscript</p><h2>Bio-LoRA</h2></div><div><h3>Biological Priors as Inductive Bias for Low-Rank Adaptation</h3><p class="manuscript-meta">2026 · Co-first author · Unpublished research manuscript</p><p>I contributed to the signal-peptide task extension, training and evaluation infrastructure, and comparisons of biologically informed adaptation methods. The work examines task-specific behavior and the controls needed to interpret it.</p><p class="muted">The manuscript was reviewed at EMNLP 2026 and was not accepted. Research details and my contribution are described in the case study.</p><div class="inline-links"><a class="text-link" href="/work/protein-language-models/">Methods &amp; contribution ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="https://openreview.net/forum?id=c2bOohFkYH" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenReview submission record ↗</a></div></div></section>
    <section class="section split"><div><p class="eyebrow">Earlier &amp; supporting work</p><h2>Related work</h2></div><div><p>My earlier NLP work involved fine-tuning multilingual encoders for Hinglish named-entity recognition and interpreting evaluations with different test scopes. More recently, FieldLens has let me investigate constrained local-model outputs, source inspection, and behavior when inference fails.</p><div class="inline-links"><a class="text-link" href="/work/hinglish-ner/">Hinglish NER ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/work/fieldlens/">FieldLens ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/work/">All work ↗</a></div></div></section>
    <p class="content-date">Research status updated 17 October 2026.</p>
  </div>
</Layout>
